{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga","id":1401490,"title":"Koldunism, the Tzimisce, and Baba Yaga","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-07T08:37:37-07:00","id":1401490,"title":"Koldunism, the Tzimisce, and Baba Yaga","content":"I am posting this as a follow-up to a conversation that I started in the &quot;Kraina/Koldunic Sorcery&quot; thread, because I think the questions I still have are both numerous and interesting enough to require their own thread, rather than derailing a topic focused more on homebrewed kraina.<br /> <br /> In the previous topic, I asked about what type of (pre-V5) Blood Sorcery Discipline Baba Yaga was most likely to practice; either Koldunic Sorcery or a predecessor to the spiritual Sielanic Thaumaturgy practiced by the Telyavelic Tremere in Lithuania. I had been resistant to the idea of Baba Yaga having Koldunic Sorcery, but ended up conceding after a little consideration. While academic exercises are fun, especially those involving WoD metaphysics and lore, my reasons for needing an answer to this are a bit more pragmatic. I have a player in a DAV20 game who is interested in playing a Baba Yaga-type forest witch Nosferatu; I am not entirely sure how metaphorical or literal this is yet, whether or not she means a serious interest in Blood Sorcery, but I want to have the best answer possible prepared if it comes to it.<br /> <br /> The thing about making Baba Yaga a Koldun is that if you imagine any of her descendants learning Blood Sorcery from her then it creates the conditions for a tradition of Nosferatu Koldun. Most of the in-game lore has depicted the Discipline as largely exclusive to the Tzimisce; the only exception I can recall is from the V20 TBH/TMR book, where the Old Clan is teaching it to Molochim Baali, of all people (that could be a whole conversation in itself, but need to stay on point). The question that matters for my game is whether or not Tzimisce Koldun would tolerate outsiders wielding the Blood Magic they have traditionally thought of as &quot;theirs,&quot; or whether a low-key retcon might be in order to have Tzimisce Koldun be aware of, and relatively ok with, Nosferatu practicing Koldunism. &quot;Tolerate&quot; and &quot;ok&quot; being relative to the obsessive hunger for knowledge and power inherent in the kraina <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It matters because I have a Tzimisce in my coterie with my Nos.<br /> <br /> And all of THAT then led me to an interesting question regarding lore; what is the origin of the Koldunic Sorcery Discipline, if both Baba Yaga and the eldest/Eldest Tzimisce are practitioners? It seems, broadly, that there are two groups of possible answers: either each group learned Koldunic Sorcery independently, or one group originally taught the other group. The lore and backstory around Baba Yaga strongly implies, if not outright states, that her Blood Sorcery was translated from the Magic or Sorcery that she practiced while alive; her having learned from the Tzimisce seems unlikely. So then, did the first Tzimisce Koldun learn from Baba Yaga, or was it an independent discovery on their part? My current fan-theory is independent discovery, with the Eldest discovering the kraina as a consequence of its/their (infernal) pact with Kupala.<br /> <br /> But I am interested in hearing opinions on my thoughts, along with the theories of others who are willing to share their ideas. So please, discuss <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T08:55:07-07:00","id":1401493,"title":"","content":"I always thought the entity known as Kupala taught the Tzimisce the secrets of Koldunic Sorcery. There\u2019s no reason Baba Yaga, being 7000+ years old, couldn\u2019t have developed a similar form of blood Sorcery, or that Kupala couldn\u2019t have taught her (for a price, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T08:56:58-07:00","id":1401494,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce learned koldunism from Kupala<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga is most likely a koldun,<br /> however, her stats present her as having thaumaturgy (that was before there were rules for koldunism, so we can't tell for certain)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T09:12:16-07:00","id":1401497,"title":"","content":"In the West the Lhiannan have their blood magic: Ogham. In the background of Baba Yaga she was a sorcerer before the Embrace. I think it's possible she created her personal magic with her knowledge. Perhaps her magic is similar to the Koldunic Sorcery, but with her power, i think could not be the case. The magic of Baba Yaga seems founded in pacts with spirits of the nature and the Wyrm (The Zmei and Koshchei). Perhaps Kupala is not the spiritual mentor of Baba Yaga, i think in another type of spirit...or demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T09:24:59-07:00","id":1401500,"title":"","content":"koldunism isn't exclusive to kupala or the tzimisce,<br /> (in mexico, there was Tlaloc that could teach koldunism),<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga probably was some kind of shaman when alive and it just became koldunism after embrace","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T09:37:17-07:00","id":1401502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401494#post1401494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce learned koldunism from Kupala<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga is most likely a koldun,<br /> however, her stats present her as having thaumaturgy (that was before there were rules for koldunism, so we can't tell for certain)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is precisely the thing. The fact that Baba Yaga's official stats list Thaumaturgy is largely meaningless in a context where no other Blood Sorcery Disciplines existed in-game yet. But again, if she did practice something more like Thaumaturgy than Koldunic Sorcery, it would likely be closer to the more spiritual variant of the Telyavs.<br /> <br /> And yes, Penelope, the Tzimisce have traditionally been depicted as learning Koldunism under the tutelage of Kupala. But none of that lore has ever been in the context of Baba Yaga (potentially) being a 9000-year old Koldun. If Baba Yaga is a Koldun, and all knowledge of Koldunism comes from Kupala, than Baba Yaga would need a pre-existing connection with Kupala. But if Koldunism is something Baba Yaga figured out &quot;on her own,&quot; then either Kupala only taught the Tzimisce something they could (in theory) have figured out &quot;on their own&quot; eventually, or it could even have been something they actually possessed before Kupala, and their extended time in Transylvania just caused a significant entanglement between the two. An added point to consider is the tendency for the WoD games to present things from a mysterious/often-IC perspective, which combined with Tzimisce pride could lead them to obscure the fact that one of their oldest traditions is something of a hand-me-down from another Clan.<br /> <br /> I have my own hypothetical answers for most/all of these questions, but hearing the opinions of people on the forums has often changed my mind, or my perspective at least, on many things. So I'm just hoping to get as much input as possible before my Nosferatu player potentially forces me to pick a hard answer, for my chronicle at least.<br /> <br /> P.S. Since there were a couple responses since my last post. I had kind of forgotten about Ogham (again), but the Discipline does seem to have some distinct qualities and requirements that make it different enough to qualify as &quot;something else,&quot; even if it evolved from Koldunic Sorcery originally.<br /> <br /> Regarding the idea of Baba Yaga's Blood Sorcery not being Koldunism or Thaumaturgy but &quot;it's own thing,&quot; that is indeed a fun idea, but also the one that would require the most effort on my part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do probably have a name for such a Discipline, however: Vedma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 07-07-2020, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T10:19:31-07:00","id":1401506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401502#post1401502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is precisely the thing. The fact that Baba Yaga's official stats list Thaumaturgy is largely meaningless in a context where no other Blood Sorcery Disciplines existed in-game yet. But again, if she did practice something more like Thaumaturgy than Koldunic Sorcery, it would likely be closer to the more spiritual variant of the Telyavs.<br /> <br /> And yes, Penelope, the Tzimisce have traditionally been depicted as learning Koldunism under the tutelage of Kupala. But none of that lore has ever been in the context of Baba Yaga (potentially) being a 9000-year old Koldun. If Baba Yaga is a Koldun, and all knowledge of Koldunism comes from Kupala, than Baba Yaga would need a pre-existing connection with Kupala. But if Koldunism is something Baba Yaga figured out &amp;quot;on her own,&amp;quot; then either Kupala only taught the Tzimisce something they could (in theory) have figured out &amp;quot;on their own&amp;quot; eventually, or it could even have been something they actually possessed before Kupala, and their extended time in Transylvania just caused a significant entanglement between the two. An added point to consider is the tendency for the WoD games to present things from a mysterious/often-IC perspective, which combined with Tzimisce pride could lead them to obscure the fact that one of their oldest traditions is something of a hand-me-down from another Clan.<br /> <br /> I have my own hypothetical answers for most/all of these questions, but hearing the opinions of people on the forums has often changed my mind, or my perspective at least, on many things. So I'm just hoping to get as much input as possible before my Nosferatu player potentially forces me to pick a hard answer, for my chronicle at least.<br /> <br /> P.S. Since there were a couple responses since my last post. I had kind of forgotten about Ogham (again), but the Discipline does seem to have some distinct qualities and requirements that make it different enough to qualify as &amp;quot;something else,&amp;quot; even if it evolved from Koldunic Sorcery originally.<br /> <br /> Regarding the idea of Baba Yaga's Blood Sorcery not being Koldunism or Thaumaturgy but &amp;quot;it's own thing,&amp;quot; that is indeed a fun idea, but also the one that would require the most effort on my part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do probably have a name for such a Discipline, however: Vedma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well thought out \ud83d\ude0a. But why couldn\u2019t Kupala and Baba Yaga have both learned Koldunic Sorcery from a common source (maybe the Dark Mother aspect of Gaia the Mother Goddess)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T10:20:23-07:00","id":1401507,"title":"","content":"Call the Dark Mother aspect Rodina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T10:21:26-07:00","id":1401508,"title":"","content":"Darker, more primal, more blood-soaked than the benign Gaia of the Garou cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T10:52:17-07:00","id":1401512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401506#post1401506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very well thought out \ud83d\ude0a. But why couldn\u2019t Kupala and Baba Yaga have both learned Koldunic Sorcery from a common source (maybe the Dark Mother aspect of Gaia the Mother Goddess)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is &quot;it depends&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As noted above, most Baba Yaga lore treats her magic as something that she developed/evolved from her shamanic practices as a mortal. She hasn't conventionally been depicted as needing a tutor in Blood Sorcery post-Embrace.<br /> <br /> Similarly, whether or not Kupala would need a tutor to &quot;learn&quot; Koldunic Sorcery depends on your in-universe answer to what Kupala *is*. Do demons that teach Dark Thaumaturgy &quot;learn&quot; the Discipline, and teach it in a conventional sense, or do they just impart knowledge or understanding supernaturally?<br /> <br /> The answer is &quot;it depends on your chronicle,&quot; but my interest has usually been in addressing the conflict between early suggestions that Kupala was a Talon of the Wyrm with later depictions making it an Earthbound. My thought has been that traditional DtF are relatively blind to the Middle Umbra, the Earthbound are depicted as changing from their roots a lot over the years. In Kupala's case, part of how it learned to make an entire mountain range into a Reliquary may have been through involvement with the Wyrm. Which would give it a connection to both the land and the Middle Umbra that could make tutoring a vampire in Blood Sorcery based on such things possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T11:29:30-07:00","id":1401520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401507#post1401507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call the Dark Mother aspect Rodina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rodina Mat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah we have evidence Kupala doesn't have a monopoly on Koldunism. In fact in V20/DV20 we learn Vampires learned Kraina in ancient times but by the founding of the Sabbat the Kolduns made a pact with Kupala and would forsake Kraina ( form of Koldunism based off of learning Kraina based off of the spirits of local regions) and learn only Koldunic Sorcery of the elements that Kupala specialized in (maybe its closer to his Demonic Lores), and they would make new Ways like the Way of Sorrow in the Koldunic Sorcery paradigm.<br /> <br /> So Baba Yaga would be a master of the Old Ways of Kraina based off of individual regions rather then the Elemental ways of Kupala.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T12:31:12-07:00","id":1401534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401512#post1401512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The short answer is &amp;quot;it depends&amp;quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As noted above, most Baba Yaga lore treats her magic as something that she developed/evolved from her shamanic practices as a mortal. She hasn't conventionally been depicted as needing a tutor in Blood Sorcery post-Embrace.<br /> <br /> Similarly, whether or not Kupala would need a tutor to &amp;quot;learn&amp;quot; Koldunic Sorcery depends on your in-universe answer to what Kupala *is*. Do demons that teach Dark Thaumaturgy &amp;quot;learn&amp;quot; the Discipline, and teach it in a conventional sense, or do they just impart knowledge or understanding supernaturally?<br /> <br /> The answer is &amp;quot;it depends on your chronicle,&amp;quot; but my interest has usually been in addressing the conflict between early suggestions that Kupala was a Talon of the Wyrm with later depictions making it an Earthbound. My thought has been that traditional DtF are relatively blind to the Middle Umbra, the Earthbound are depicted as changing from their roots a lot over the years. In Kupala's case, part of how it learned to make an entire mountain range into a Reliquary may have been through involvement with the Wyrm. Which would give it a connection to both the land and the Middle Umbra that could make tutoring a vampire in Blood Sorcery based on such things possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, maybe. But I still think Baba Yaga\u2019s Blood Sorcery is a natural outgrowth of her shamanic Earthmother worship in life, not something she learned from a demon or a Wyrm-creature. You can use Koldunic Sorcery to represent it cause it\u2019s basically easier than making up a whole new system, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019re 100% the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T12:32:46-07:00","id":1401535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401520#post1401520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rodina Mat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah we have evidence Kupala doesn't have a monopoly on Koldunism. In fact in V20/DV20 we learn Vampires learned Kraina in ancient times but by the founding of the Sabbat the Kolduns made a pact with Kupala and would forsake Kraina ( form of Koldunism based off of learning Kraina based off of the spirits of local regions) and learn only Koldunic Sorcery of the elements that Kupala specialized in (maybe its closer to his Demonic Lores), and they would make new Ways like the Way of Sorrow in the Koldunic Sorcery paradigm.<br /> <br /> So Baba Yaga would be a master of the Old Ways of Kraina based off of individual regions rather then the Elemental ways of Kupala.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Idk all that, but that definitely supports my argument above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T15:02:42-07:00","id":1401563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401534#post1401534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, maybe. But I still think Baba Yaga\u2019s Blood Sorcery is a natural outgrowth of her shamanic Earthmother worship in life, not something she learned from a demon or a Wyrm-creature. You can use Koldunic Sorcery to represent it cause it\u2019s basically easier than making up a whole new system, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019re 100% the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted in Eldagusto's post, there's a distinction between old-school kraina Koldunism versus modern/Kupalan, and I agree that Baba Yaga would practice the former <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That being said, I use Gaia both to refer to the Incarna of Earth, and the 'Ultimate Spirit' of which the Triat are just parts, so &quot;Dark Gaian&quot; and &quot;Wyrmish&quot; are closer in my books than some might reckon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T16:22:47-07:00","id":1401570,"title":"","content":"Okay. That makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T18:08:14-07:00","id":1401584,"title":"","content":"Of note, Baba Yaga has made alliances with several &quot;demons&quot; notably the tzmei and koschei. Some of her magic may run more to the dark side. It was not uncommon for shamans to learn some of their magic from a spirit, ancestor or guide. Baba Yaga may have learned some of her thaum from the &quot;devils&quot; she summoned. That, of course is only speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T18:09:34-07:00","id":1401585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401563#post1401563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As noted in Eldagusto's post, there's a distinction between old-school kraina Koldunism versus modern/Kupalan, and I agree that Baba Yaga would practice the former <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That being said, I use Gaia both to refer to the Incarna of Earth, and the 'Ultimate Spirit' of which the Triat are just parts, so &quot;Dark Gaian&quot; and &quot;Wyrmish&quot; are closer in my books than some might reckon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have Gaia as the Celestine of Earth and Earth alone. It's just the Garou have a tendency to inflate their own importance and the importance of their religion. She's not even as important as Helios who is just one star spirit among trillions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T19:44:16-07:00","id":1401601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401534#post1401534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, maybe. But I still think Baba Yaga\u2019s Blood Sorcery is a natural outgrowth of her shamanic Earthmother worship in life, not something she learned from a demon or a Wyrm-creature. You can use Koldunic Sorcery to represent it cause it\u2019s basically easier than making up a whole new system, but I don\u2019t think they\u2019re 100% the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider another option. Assamite sorcery may be older than Koldunism. It is certainly much older than the concept of the &quot;Middle east&quot;. It will at least go back to the Mesopotamian city-states. Marduk and Tanith, king Shulgi of Ur and Sennacherib. Sumerian civilization started in the fifth millennium BC. Just on the other side of the Caucasus and Zardos mountains was a complicated patchwork of peoples and nations. This area, towards the Pontic-Caspian steppe is possibly where Baba Yaga was embraced in 5000 BC. Further north you have hunter-gatherers. Which may or may not fit with her background.<br /> <br /> My point is that she was as close to the Sumerian traditions as she was to the Transylvanian, and with less in the way of mind-bogglingly densely populated territories between her and the Sumerians. She was embraced at the right time and possibly close to the right place to be part of the beginnings there. If she came into the night from a life of shamanic magic, it is possible she would have exchanged knowledge with the early Sumerian bloodmages, and been part of the early development of Dur-An-Ki. It would be a very diverged an primordial form of it though.<br /> <br /> She may have had a complicated relationship with Ur-Shulgi when the world was younger. She was born to light and goodness and beauty. He was the absolute opposite, and yet they ended up quite similar.<br /> <br /> Hey, anyone remember if we ever knew what the little grandmothers end game was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T20:03:05-07:00","id":1401604,"title":"","content":"Mechanically I would use Koldunism and a few other Paths of Thaumaturgy that are thematically appropriate, like Weather Control.<br /> <br /> For Baba Yaga, I would not use Kupala as the spirit mentor who provided her that knowledge. I think it works best for her to have her own patron, and thus her knowledge is a separate legacy even if mechanically the same. In that case, you can select a name from some of the other East Slavic gods as a representation of a Kupala-like figure which you can then translate into whatever fits your needs (actual pagan goddess,Incarna spirit, demon, Great Old One, whatever). But remember that Baba Yaga predates the Slavs by thousands of years, and therefore the name of the entity she learned anything from would be something quite different when Baba Yaga encountered it. But that entity might be known by an East Slavic name today. I would pick some variant of Morana/Marena/Marzanna/Mara, but there are many other that would be thematically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T21:17:10-07:00","id":1401614,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone for your replies!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401584#post1401584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of note, Baba Yaga has made alliances with several &quot;demons&quot; notably the tzmei and koschei. Some of her magic may run more to the dark side. It was not uncommon for shamans to learn some of their magic from a spirit, ancestor or guide. Baba Yaga may have learned some of her thaum from the &quot;devils&quot; she summoned. That, of course is only speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! It was a long time back, so I would need to refresh my memory to be sure, but I believe it was in Rage Across Russia that I read the &quot;myth&quot; of Baba Yaga's Embrace by the Nos Antediluvian, with her summoning the Zmei (and perhaps Koschei as well, memory fails there) to aid her in vengeance. In the myth at least, she seemed to just spontaneously convert her old ways to Blood Sorcery. The actual details could vary, but it definitely suggests the possibility <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401585#post1401585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have Gaia as the Celestine of Earth and Earth alone. It's just the Garou have a tendency to inflate their own importance and the importance of their religion. She's not even as important as Helios who is just one star spirit among trillions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed 100%. My using the name 'Gaia' for &quot;Big Gaia&quot; as well as Celestine &quot;Little Gaia&quot; is just a concession to the game's tendency to conflate the two; given the generally out-of-touch nature of &quot;Big G,&quot; don't see the need to come up with something different. Any time the Garou/Fera have said &quot;Gaia told us to&quot; and they weren't wrong or lying, it was &quot;Little G&quot; in my canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It serves both my taste for nihilism and the needs of my crossover addiction, making compatibility with Mage easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401601#post1401601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consider another option. Assamite sorcery may be older than Koldunism. It is certainly much older than the concept of the &quot;Middle east&quot;. It will at least go back to the Mesopotamian city-states. Marduk and Tanith, king Shulgi of Ur and Sennacherib. Sumerian civilization started in the fifth millennium BC. Just on the other side of the Caucasus and Zardos mountains was a complicated patchwork of peoples and nations. This area, towards the Pontic-Caspian steppe is possibly where Baba Yaga was embraced in 5000 BC. Further north you have hunter-gatherers. Which may or may not fit with her background.<br /> <br /> My point is that she was as close to the Sumerian traditions as she was to the Transylvanian, and with less in the way of mind-bogglingly densely populated territories between her and the Sumerians. She was embraced at the right time and possibly close to the right place to be part of the beginnings there. If she came into the night from a life of shamanic magic, it is possible she would have exchanged knowledge with the early Sumerian bloodmages, and been part of the early development of Dur-An-Ki. It would be a very diverged an primordial form of it though.<br /> <br /> She may have had a complicated relationship with Ur-Shulgi when the world was younger. She was born to light and goodness and beauty. He was the absolute opposite, and yet they ended up quite similar.<br /> <br /> Hey, anyone remember if we ever knew what the little grandmothers end game was?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of her having a connection to Ur-Shulgi is interesting, but for the most part I'm not interested in having her involved with more southern areas. As noted, this topic started when I posed the question of whether or not Koldunism was the most appropriate for Baba Yaga, and the reason I ended up agreeing was twofold. Firstly, Koldunism is a relatively &quot;spiritual&quot; form of Blood Sorcery, even if this hasn't been fleshed out much in crossover terms (VtM-Umbra crossover rules for Koldunism are my idea of the good time xD); but Dur-An-Ki also has that going for it. What persuaded me that Baba Yaga should be a Koldun, or a primordial-ur-equivalent, is the connection to land and territory; it's a very distinct feature of Koldunism, and it's a distinct feature of Baba Yaga's portrayal.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the actual sources on this, or can't recall them, but what I recall reading of Baba Yaga's &quot;end game&quot; was a desire to continue controlling, and &quot;protecting,&quot; her homeland. The Shadow Curtain was, definitely metaphorically and possibly literally, a manifestation of Baba Yaga's attachment to &quot;her land.&quot; I don't think they have made a Blood Sorcery Discipline yet that depicts that better than Koldunic Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401604#post1401604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically I would use Koldunism and a few other Paths of Thaumaturgy that are thematically appropriate, like Weather Control.<br /> <br /> For Baba Yaga, I would not use Kupala as the spirit mentor who provided her that knowledge. I think it works best for her to have her own patron, and thus her knowledge is a separate legacy even if mechanically the same. In that case, you can select a name from some of the other East Slavic gods as a representation of a Kupala-like figure which you can then translate into whatever fits your needs (actual pagan goddess,Incarna spirit, demon, Great Old One, whatever). But remember that Baba Yaga predates the Slavs by thousands of years, and therefore the name of the entity she learned anything from would be something quite different when Baba Yaga encountered it. But that entity might be known by an East Slavic name today. I would pick some variant of Morana/Marena/Marzanna/Mara, but there are many other that would be thematically appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed about the form of Koldunism practiced by Baba Yaga, and possibly her descendants, would not be centred around Kupala (unless they were learning Carpathian kraina at some point), but around different Slavic deities and mythic figures. But as referred to above, I remember her original conversion of her shaman ways to Blood Sorcery involving Wyrm spirits, so I'm inclined to draw a connection there, even if she's not a (knowing) servant of the Wyrm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T21:24:28-07:00","id":1401616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401584#post1401584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of note, Baba Yaga has made alliances with several &quot;demons&quot; notably the tzmei and koschei. Some of her magic may run more to the dark side. It was not uncommon for shamans to learn some of their magic from a spirit, ancestor or guide. Baba Yaga may have learned some of her thaum from the &quot;devils&quot; she summoned. That, of course is only speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Tzimisce and Baba Yaga may have something there that the Wyrm isn't actually corrupted. It's just antithetical to life.<br /> <br /> So, of course the Spirits of Entropy and Decay and Corruption will like vampires.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that's the Mage view of the Triat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T04:57:01-07:00","id":1401662,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2471\" data-vbnamecard=\"2471\">Trollroot</a> agreed. I Liked your posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:25:32-07:00","id":1401687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401616#post1401616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Tzimisce and Baba Yaga may have something there that the Wyrm isn't actually corrupted. It's just antithetical to life.<br /> <br /> So, of course the Spirits of Entropy and Decay and Corruption will like vampires.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that's the Mage view of the Triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. I've generally taken the story of the &quot;corruption&quot; of the Weaver and the Wyrm at face value for the most part, but through the lens that &quot;corruption&quot; from the perspective of us is simply the presence of illness/dysfunction in cosmic-scale entities, rather than being about &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil.&quot; But the idea that a perfectly &quot;natural&quot; shift in the balance of the Triat comes across as &quot;corruption&quot; to the Garou, given their own ties to different (diminishing) aspects of the cosmic nature, is also interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:29:19-07:00","id":1401689,"title":"","content":"Yes, but Entropy and Corruption aren\u2019t the same thing. One is morally neutral, one isn\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:52:02-07:00","id":1401693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401689#post1401689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Entropy and Corruption aren\u2019t the same thing. One is morally neutral, one isn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem would be assuming that the Triat would have any care about morality. They are beings that are very arguably above good and evil.<br /> <br /> Wyrm corruption can lead to a person becoming suicidal, a drug addict, or a serial killer.<br /> <br /> However, the end result is just more &quot;decay&quot; that causes things to break down--which is just part of the cosmic procedure.<br /> <br /> A storm or plague does not care about morality. It simply is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-08-2020, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T11:14:27-07:00","id":1401718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401689#post1401689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Entropy and Corruption aren\u2019t the same thing. One is morally neutral, one isn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely the point.<br /> <br /> That's why &quot;corruption&quot; was in quotes all the time. As CTPhipps points out, what is regarded as &quot;unnatural corruption&quot; by the individual who suffers for it is inconsequential to the larger or &quot;higher&quot; entity for whom it is just a natural function.<br /> <br /> Reverse scale example: cancer. If I call another person a &quot;cancer&quot; on society, most would regard that as a moral judgment. But literal cancer isn't good or evil, and it didn't choose to be cancer; it just is what it is. Now compare the human &quot;cancer&quot;; we can declare an individual's actions to be &quot;cancerous&quot; to the &quot;body&quot; of our society, but that's frequently just a judgment made by individuals who have defined the &quot;greater good&quot; as their interests. Even if that's not the case, is it truly fair to judge our human &quot;cancer,&quot; morally speaking, if their being such was largely determined by factors outside their control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:31:08-07:00","id":1401732,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> hmmm, interesting. But then how would you distinguish between the current Corrupted Wyrm and the original Balance Wyrm? Or would you say there is no difference?<br /> <br /> Sorry to hijack the thread, but now I\u2019m curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:44:30-07:00","id":1401735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401732#post1401732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> hmmm, interesting. But then how would you distinguish between the current Corrupted Wyrm and the original Balance Wyrm? Or would you say there is no difference?<br /> <br /> Sorry to hijack the thread, but now I\u2019m curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which gets to the heart of the matter.<br /> <br /> IS the Wyrm corrupted or is it just doing what it's supposed to do?<br /> <br /> What is part of the system doesn't necessarily benefit humanity or the Garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:38:49-07:00","id":1401750,"title":"","content":"Wow! I never thought of it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:09:50-07:00","id":1401797,"title":"","content":"I would say the Wyrm is corrupted. Mainly because it dialed up its mandate to unnecessarily extreme levels. It used to destroy only things that no longer served a purpose. Now it wants everything gone. <br /> <br /> Also, I wouldn't say that Baba Yaga made a deal with Koschei so much that she freaked out during her fight with Absimiliard and unlocked the cage to a rabid beast in hope of getting away.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm sure that while living Baba Yaga practiced something akin to Koldunism. But wasn't taught through Kupala. She was centered in Russia and Kupala is centered in the Carpathian mountains. Koldunic Sorcery is similar to other forms of shamanistic magic in that it uses the spirits of the land to work. Native Americans had that 10,000 years ago as well and didn't have dealings with Kupala. It's not a reach that her own pre-embrace shamanism is separate from Kupala.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T23:20:33-07:00","id":1401860,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s true. Geographically Transylvania and the Rodina (the Russian Motherland) are hundreds of miles apart (and quite distinct culturally as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T01:15:42-07:00","id":1401872,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't think Thaumaturgy or Blood Sorcery is really any single distinct Discipline.<br /> <br /> Setite Thaumaturgy is going to be different from Assamite Thaumaturgy from Tremere Thaumaturgy from Baba Yaga's Thaumaturgy and Koldunism.<br /> <br /> Really, the big similarity is the fact Baba Yaga and the Tzimisce both place a lot of emphasis on Earth, spirit, and nature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T06:09:58-07:00","id":1401911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401490-koldunism-the-tzimisce-and-baba-yaga?p=1401872#post1401872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't think Thaumaturgy or Blood Sorcery is really any single distinct Discipline.<br /> <br /> Setite Thaumaturgy is going to be different from Assamite Thaumaturgy from Tremere Thaumaturgy from Baba Yaga's Thaumaturgy and Koldunism.<br /> <br /> Really, the big similarity is the fact Baba Yaga and the Tzimisce both place a lot of emphasis on Earth, spirit, and nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm probably somewhere in the middle. The different Blood Sorcery Disciplines are distinct enough that practitioners of one particular &quot;style&quot; or &quot;paradigm&quot; can't just pick up another style's rituals or Paths. But, in most cases, there is enough in common that stuff can be translated over, with effort.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga practicing Koldunism fits because of the connections to Spirit and land, as you note. What she practices may differ from Tzimisce Koldunism to an extent comparable to different schools of Thaumaturgy, but there seems little cause for much distinction in crunch.<br /> <br /> New prompt: how might one want to change the mechanics of Baba Yaga's Blood Sorcery to distinguish from the Tzimisce brand, beyond just different kraina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}